cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CARVE: Cluster Analysis with Resampling for Validation and Exploration"
abstract: >-
  CARVE chooses the number of clusters and the clustering method by
  resampling. Every candidate configuration clusters many subsamples of the
  data and is scored for stability, the agreement between the clusterings of
  two overlapping subsamples, and for generalizability, how well a classifier
  trained on one subsample predicts the clusters of the held-out samples.
  The repository has a Python package, carve-validate, and an R package,
  CARVE.
